<strong>Example 2:</strong></p><pre>Input: n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]]\nOutput: 1</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p><pre>Input: n = 3, edges = []\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: Each node is its own component.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p><ul><li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 2000</code></li><li><code>0 &lt;= edges.length &lt;= 5000</code></li><li><code>edges[i].length == 2</code></li><li><code>0 &lt;= a, b &lt; n</code></li><li><code>a != b</code></li><li><code>No edge appears twice</code></li></ul>","exampleTestcases":"5\n[[0,1],[1,2],[3,4]]\n5\n[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]]\n3\n[]","metaData":"{\"name\": \"countComponents\", \"params\": [{\"name\": \"n\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"name\": \"edges\", \"type\": \"integer[][]\"}], \"return\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}","codeSnippets":[{"langSlug":"python3","code":"class Solution:\n    def countComponents(self, n: int, edges: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        \n"}]}}